            <header class="about-head record-hero">
              <h1>About this Record.</h1>
              <p>The Co-Existence Record is a living, source-linked public record from Co-Existing with AI. It turns long conversations into questions people can explore without losing the original context.</p>
            </header>
            <div class="about-grid">
              <section><h2>Start with a question.</h2><p>Each question gathers positions into shared ground, different views, and what remains open. The map shows disagreement without forcing a single conclusion.</p></section>
              <section><h2>Check the source.</h2><p>Every published position links to the speaker, timestamp, surrounding exchange, and original recording so readers can inspect the record themselves.</p></section>
              <section><h2>Challenge the map.</h2><p>CIF welcomes corrections, missing evidence, and competing interpretations. Substantive corrections will remain visible in the Record’s change history.</p></section>
              <section><h2>Public by default.</h2><p>No paywall, required email, or institutional affiliation. If institutions later help fund, host, or extend the work, access will remain public.</p></section>
            </div>
